<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Highest/Lowest Australian P-E Ratios-Jan 28.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Highest/Lowest Australian P-E Ratios-Jan 28.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-01-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Highest and lowest price earnings ratios for Australian companies included in the 320-company All Ordinaries Index based on closing prices on Friday. P/E based on rolling 12 months earnings.</p>
<p>Highest 10</p>
<p>Rank Name		     P/E    Close</p>
<p> 1   Portman Min	   352.38   2.22</p>
<p> 2   Niugini Min	   214.39   2.98</p>
<p> 3   Countrywide-PP	188.71   1.17</p>
<p> 4   Mayne Nickless	173.29   7.85</p>
<p> 5   Colonial Coml	 121.31   2.22</p>
<p> 6   Adel Bton Cement    115.94   1.60</p>
<p> 7   Forrestania Gold     89.61   2.50</p>
<p> 8   Herald Rsc	     84.96   0.96</p>
<p> 9   Energy Equity	  79.86   1.11</p>
<p>10   Westral Forest	 78.26   2.16</p>
<p>Lowest 10</p>
<p> 1   Dominion Min	    2.02   0.88</p>
<p> 2   Consol Rutile	   3.54   0.86</p>
<p> 3   Premier Inv	     4.62   0.82</p>
<p> 4   BTR Plc		   6.23   5.80</p>
<p> 5   Parbury Ltd	     6.33   0.75</p>
<p> 6   OLS Asia Hldgs	  6.72   0.80</p>
<p> 7   Aust Gold Rsc	   7.12   1.30</p>
<p> 8   Renison Goldflds	7.60   5.24</p>
<p> 9   Capcount Prop	   7.87   0.86</p>
<p>10   Templeton Global	7.88   1.38</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 373-1800</p>
</text>
